  "id": "conventional-level",
  "term": "conventional level",
  "definition": "In Kohlberg’s model of moral development, the conventional level is a way of judging moral issues mainly by following laws, rules, and social order. It reflects moral reasoning centered on maintaining norms rather than on broader shared principles.",
